          "description": "In the heel twist the weight sits back on the heels and the toes fan out and in. It feels heavier and more grounded than the toe twist, and alternating the two — toes, heels, toes, heels — lets the feet walk sideways across the floor. Many combos switch between them to change texture without changing tempo.",
