          "summary": "A heel dig out on the diagonal, back in, then a knee up — alternating sides.",
          "description": "The farmer is a classic house step built from a heel dig and a knee lift. The free foot digs its heel out on a diagonal, comes back in, and the opposite knee lifts before the pattern repeats on the other side. It has a steady, stomping character that sits well on tracks with a heavy kick. Teachers vary the details — some add a hop, some cross the heel in front — so learn the basic shape and watch the video for the version shown.",
