          "description": "Happy feet is quick alternating footwork on the balls of the feet, done with loose ankles and knees so the feet seem to patter over the floor. It is often used to fill a phrase with energy, to cover a transition, or to travel a short distance quickly. Speed is the point, but only if it stays even and on the music.",
